{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives."}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"title":"Sending batches","anchor":"Sending-batches"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch"],"title":"Encoding a batch","anchor":"Encoding-a-batch"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportResponse"],"title":"Reading a 2xx answer","anchor":"Reading-a-2xx-answer"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchRequests","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/SkippedRecord"],"title":"Splitting a batch into requests","anchor":"Splitting-a-batch-into-requests"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/TransientStatus","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidTransientStatus"],"title":"Retrying a vendor’s own statuses","anchor":"Retrying-a-vendors-own-statuses"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/InvalidBackoff","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry"],"title":"Waiting between attempts","anchor":"Waiting-between-attempts"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError"],"title":"Sending requests","anchor":"Sending-requests"}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"externalID":"HTTPDestinations","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"HTTPDestinations","symbolKind":"module"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/httpdestinations"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is a destination that posts each batch it receives as the requests its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" splits it into: one request for an endpoint without limits. Each body is whatever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the encoder writes for its records, so events need no "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance and the wire format is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"yours. It sends with "},{"code":"URLSession","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/URLSessionTransport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" by default, or through any "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" you pass."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A send that gets no response, or a 5xx, 408 or 429 status, is sent again after the next wait of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff"},{"type":"text","text":": nominally 1 second, doubling up to 60 seconds, unless you pass another. So"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is one answered with a status the encoder lists in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses"},{"type":"text","text":", which every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoder declares: empty for most servers, or each other failure its vendor answers to a request"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"worth sending again, such as Aptabase’s 418 for a slow upload."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A 2xx counts as delivered unless the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" reads its body and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"says otherwise. Some vendors answer 200 to a request they didn’t store, and say so only in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"body: Mixpanel’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"{\"status\": 0}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or Aptabase’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"{\"error\": ...}","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for an unknown key. A 2xx the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder reads as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/rejected(reason:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is dropped and reported as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport\/rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":". One it reads as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/transient(reason:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" is sent again under the same backoff and deadline as a 5xx.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"An encoder should count an empty body, or one it can’t read, as delivered, so an answer it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"doesn’t recognize never sends a request again and again; the DestinationTesting conformance kit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checks that it does. A transient answer is retried until the request’s deadline, so an encoder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whose requests have none should return rejected instead.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each wait has full jitter by default: a random wait shorter than the nominal one, so apps refused","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"at the same moment retry at different moments. Pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/Jitter-swift.enum\/none"},{"text":" for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"nominal waits. In tests, pass a seeded generator as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"randomNumberGenerator:"},{"text":" for jittered waits","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that repeat from one run to the next, as long as one request retries at a time: copies of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination retrying at once share the generator’s draws in the order they ask for them. Never","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"seed it in production, where every device would then wait the same, which defeats the jitter. The","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destination takes the next batch only once this one is delivered or dropped, so a tracker’s store","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps the batch’s records until then. A batch the endpoint answers with any other status, whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request can never be sent, or that the encoder can’t encode is dropped, logged and reported on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports"},{"text":" as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"},{"text":", as is each record the encoder leaves out","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of its requests. So is a request still undelivered at its ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline"},{"text":", which an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"encoder sets for a vendor that misdates or ignores old events: the destination checks it on its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"now:"},{"text":" clock before every attempt and sends nothing more once it has passed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The tracing instrument injects the trace context of each request’s first record into its header","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fields, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is always the encoder’s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reach for this module to send to a server whose format you write yourself. For TraffluentCollector’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"format, give the destination a "},{"code":"CollectorBatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"CollectorEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); for PostHog,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"make it with "},{"code":"HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken:host:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"PostHogEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Amplitude, with "},{"code":"HTTPDestination.amplitude(apiKey:region:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"AmplitudeEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Mixpanel, with "},{"code":"HTTPDestination.mixpanel(projectToken:region:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"MixpanelEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":");"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for Segment, RudderStack or Customer.io Data Pipelines, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"HTTPDestination.segment(writeKey:region:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"SegmentSpecEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Google Analytics 4, from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"server, with "},{"code":"HTTPDestination.googleAnalytics(measurementID:apiSecret:region:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"GoogleAnalyticsEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Snowplow, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"HTTPDestination.snowplow(collector:vendor:appID:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"SnowplowEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"TelemetryDeck, with "},{"code":"HTTPDestination.telemetryDeck(appID:namespace:testMode:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"TelemetryDeckEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Matomo, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"HTTPDestination.matomo(url:siteID:dimensions:category:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"MatomoEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Heap, with "},{"code":"HTTPDestination.heap(appID:region:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"HeapEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); for Aptabase, with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"HTTPDestination.aptabase(appKey:host:isDebug:plan:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"AptabaseEncoding","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"). To read events"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside the app or in a test, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"InMemoryDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"code":"Destinations","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") instead."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import HTTPDestinations","","struct PlansEncoder: BatchEncoder {","    static let transientStatuses: Set<TransientStatus> = []","","    static func outcome(of response: HTTPTransportResponse, for request: EncodedRequest) -> ResponseOutcome {","        .delivered","    }","","    func requests(for batch: [EventRecord]) -> BatchRequests<Never> {","        let plans = batch.compactMap { ($0.event as? SignedUp)?.plan }","        let body = EncodedBatch(body: Data(plans.joined(separator: \"\\n\").utf8), contentType: \"text\/plain\")","        return BatchRequests(requests: [EncodedRequest(body: body, recordIDs: batch.map(\\.id))], skippedRecords: [])","    }","}","","let server = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: endpointURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder(),","    backoff: try ExponentialBackoff(initialDelay: .seconds(2), maximumDelay: .seconds(120)))","let drops = server.dropReports","let watching = Task {","    for await drop in drops {","        print(\"Dropped a batch: \\(drop)\")","    }","}","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: server)"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers this destination beside the others, and what a delivery does while a batch is retried."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchRequests":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BatchRequests","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A batch as ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","isActive":true},{"text":" encodes it: the requests that carry its records, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the records it left out.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchrequests","role":"symbol","title":"BatchRequests","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchRequests","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BatchRequests","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ResponseOutcome/rejected(reason:)":{"title":"ResponseOutcome.rejected(reason:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The vendor stored none of the request’s records, and wouldn’t if it were sent again, for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reason"},{"type":"text","text":", the vendor’s own words where its body has them: "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" drops the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"request and reports it as "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport\/rejectedInBody(status:reason:recordIDs:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"rejected"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"reason"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/responseoutcome\/rejected(reason:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome\/rejected(reason:)"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/BatchEncoder/transientStatuses":{"fragments":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"transientStatuses","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations15TransientStatusV","text":"TransientStatus","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The failure statuses, beyond 408 Request Timeout, 429 Too Many Requests and every 5xx, that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" sends a request of this encoder again after: ","type":"text"},{"code":"[]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for none.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/batchencoder\/transientstatuses","required":true,"role":"symbol","title":"transientStatuses","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/transientStatuses","type":"topic"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ResponseOutcome":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/responseoutcome","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a successful (2xx) answer to a request means, as its "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" reads the answer’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"body ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/outcome(of:for:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"title":"ResponseOutcome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResponseOutcome"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResponseOutcome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ResponseOutcome"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/NonPositiveRetry":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NonPositiveRetry"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The error ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/delay(beforeRetry:)","isActive":true},{"text":" throws for a retry numbered below 1.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/nonpositiveretry","role":"symbol","title":"NonPositiveRetry","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/NonPositiveRetry","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"NonPositiveRetry"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/SkippedRecord":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A record a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" left out of a batch’s requests, and why.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/skippedrecord","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/SkippedRecord","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SkippedRecord"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SkippedRecord"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SkippedRecord","role":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/HTTPTransportResponse":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/httptransportresponse","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPTransportResponse","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"What an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"text":" received for a request: the response’s status and header fields, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its body.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportResponse","title":"HTTPTransportResponse","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"HTTPTransportResponse","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/EncodedBatch":{"title":"EncodedBatch","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EncodedBatch"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A batch encoded as a request body: its bytes, and the media type that says how to read them.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/encodedbatch","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EncodedBatch"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/EncodedRequest/deadline":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedRequest\/deadline","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The latest wall-clock time at which the request may be sent, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when it may be sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at any time."}],"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deadline","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:20FoundationEssentials4DateV","text":"Date","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations\/encodedrequest\/deadline","kind":"symbol","title":"deadline"},"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations/ExponentialBackoff/delay(beforeRetry:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/ExponentialBackoff\/delay(beforeRetry:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The nominal wait before retry number ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"retry"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"initialDelay"},{"text":" doubled ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"retry - 1"},{"text":" times, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maximumDelay"},{"text":" if that is less.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"delay"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"beforeRetry"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"